<!DOCTYPE html>
{# AgentGuardian PDF report — enterprise redesign.

   Executive-dashboard light theme (cream paper, purple brand, severity-coded
   spines). WeasyPrint-safe: block + tables + floats, no JS, no flex page
   breaks. Fonts are embedded as WOFF2 in this template's fonts/ directory and
   resolved by WeasyPrint via the template loader's base path.

   Sections:
     1. Cover            — product mark, scan id/target/date, big AIVSS + band
     2. Executive summary — posture paragraph + KPI card row
     3. Overview          — scan-plan definition tables + ASI coverage table
     4. Findings          — severity-coded cards with chips + evidence
     5. Appendices        — A triple-framework map, B methodology, C receipt

   Rendered by reports/pdf.py:_render_weasyprint with: scan, findings,
   asi_rows, band_colour. Severity counts / KPI values are derived inline. #}
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <title>AgentGuardian scan {{ scan.id }}</title>
    <style>
      /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ *
       * Embedded fonts (do not change names/paths — resolved by WeasyPrint) *
       * ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
      @font-face {
        font-family: "Inter";
        src: url("fonts/Inter-Regular.woff2") format("woff2");
        font-weight: 400;
        font-style: normal;
      }
      @font-face {
        font-family: "Inter";
        src: url("fonts/Inter-Bold.woff2") format("woff2");
        font-weight: 700;
        font-style: normal;
      }
      @font-face {
        font-family: "JetBrains Mono";
        src: url("fonts/JetBrainsMono-Regular.woff2") format("woff2");
        font-weight: 400;
        font-style: normal;
      }
      {# Source Serif Pro is requested for headlines. If the WOFF2 is not yet
         dropped into fonts/, WeasyPrint falls back to the serif stack below —
         layout is unaffected. The @font-face is declared optimistically. #}
      @font-face {
        font-family: "Source Serif Pro";
        src: url("fonts/SourceSerifPro-Regular.woff2") format("woff2");
        font-weight: 400;
        font-style: normal;
      }
      @font-face {
        font-family: "Source Serif Pro";
        src: url("fonts/SourceSerifPro-SemiBold.woff2") format("woff2");
        font-weight: 600;
        font-style: normal;
      }

      /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ *
       * Theme tokens (executive dashboard, light)                          *
       * ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
      :root {
        --exec-bg:        #fafaf7;
        --card:           #ffffff;
        --sunken:         #f4f1ea;
        --ink:            #1a1a1a;
        --ink-muted:      #525252;
        --ink-subtle:     #8a8a8a;
        --border:         #e8e6e0;
        --border-strong:  #d8d5cc;
        --brand:          #8b5cf6;
        --brand-strong:   #7c3aed;
        --brand-tint:     #f3eeff;
        --crit:    #b91c1c; --crit-bg: #fef2f2;
        --high:    #d97706; --high-bg: #fff7ed;
        --med:     #ca8a04; --med-bg:  #fefce8;
        --low:     #65a30d; --low-bg:  #f7fee7;
        --info:    #0ea5e9;
      }

      /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ *
       * Paged-media: running footer + page counter                         *
       * ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
      @page {
        size: Letter;
        margin: 0.85in 0.75in 0.95in 0.75in;
        background: #fafaf7;
        @bottom-left {
          content: "AgentGuardian  ·  Scan {{ scan.id }}";
          font-family: "JetBrains Mono", "SF Mono", "Menlo", monospace;
          font-size: 7.5pt;
          color: #8a8a8a;
          padding-bottom: 2mm;
        }
        @bottom-right {
          content: counter(page) " / " counter(pages);
          font-family: "JetBrains Mono", "SF Mono", "Menlo", monospace;
          font-size: 7.5pt;
          color: #8a8a8a;
          padding-bottom: 2mm;
        }
        @bottom-center {
          content: "CONFIDENTIAL — SECURITY ASSESSMENT";
          font-family: "JetBrains Mono", "SF Mono", "Menlo", monospace;
          font-size: 6.5pt;
          letter-spacing: 0.12em;
          color: #b8b4aa;
          padding-bottom: 2mm;
        }
      }
      @page :first {
        margin: 0;
        @bottom-left   { content: ""; }
        @bottom-right  { content: ""; }
        @bottom-center { content: ""; }
      }

      /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ *
       * Base typography                                                    *
       * ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
      html { background: var(--exec-bg); }
      body {
        font-family: "Inter", -apple-system, "Segoe UI", "Helvetica Neue", "Arial", sans-serif;
        color: var(--ink);
        background: var(--exec-bg);
        line-height: 1.55;
        font-size: 9.5pt;
        margin: 0;
        -weasy-hyphens: none;
      }
      h1, h2, h3, h4 {
        font-family: "Source Serif Pro", "Georgia", "Times New Roman", serif;
        color: var(--ink);
        font-weight: 600;
        margin: 0;
      }
      p { margin: 0 0 0.7em; }
      a { color: var(--brand-strong); text-decoration: none; }
      strong { font-weight: 700; }

      .eyebrow {
        font-family: "JetBrains Mono", "SF Mono", "Menlo", monospace;
        font-size: 7.5pt;
        font-weight: 400;
        letter-spacing: 0.22em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        color: var(--brand-strong);
        margin: 0 0 0.5em;
      }
      .mono, code, pre {
        font-family: "JetBrains Mono", "SF Mono", "Menlo", "Consolas", monospace;
      }
      .muted { color: var(--ink-muted); }
      .subtle { color: var(--ink-subtle); }

      /* Section scaffolding */
      section.block {
        padding: 0.2in 0 0.05in;
      }
      .section-head {
        border-bottom: 1.5px solid var(--border-strong);
        padding-bottom: 0.5em;
        margin-bottom: 1em;
      }
      .section-head h2 {
        font-size: 17pt;
        line-height: 1.15;
        letter-spacing: -0.01em;
      }
      .section-head .lede {
        margin: 0.35em 0 0;
        color: var(--ink-muted);
        font-size: 9.5pt;
        max-width: 6.3in;
      }

      /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ *
       * Cover                                                              *
       * ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
      .cover {
        page-break-after: always;
        height: 11in;
        background: var(--exec-bg);
        position: relative;
        padding: 0;
      }
      .cover-inner {
        position: absolute;
        top: 1.1in; left: 0.9in; right: 0.9in; bottom: 0.9in;
      }
      .cover-rule {
        height: 4px;
        background: var(--brand);
        width: 0.9in;
        margin-bottom: 0.4in;
      }
      .cover-mark {
        font-family: "JetBrains Mono", "SF Mono", monospace;
        font-size: 11pt;
        letter-spacing: 0.32em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        color: var(--ink);
        font-weight: 400;
      }
      .cover-mark .dot { color: var(--brand); }
      .cover-kicker {
        margin-top: 0.18in;
        font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace;
        font-size: 8pt;
        letter-spacing: 0.18em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        color: var(--ink-subtle);
      }
      .cover-title {
        margin-top: 1.5in;
        font-size: 34pt;
        line-height: 1.08;
        letter-spacing: -0.02em;
        color: var(--ink);
        max-width: 6in;
      }
      .cover-score-wrap {
        margin-top: 0.55in;
        padding: 0;
      }
      .cover-score {
        font-family: "Source Serif Pro", "Georgia", serif;
        font-weight: 600;
        font-size: 96pt;
        line-height: 0.9;
        color: {{ band_colour }};
        letter-spacing: -0.03em;
      }
      .cover-score .denom {
        font-size: 26pt;
        color: var(--ink-subtle);
        letter-spacing: 0;
      }
      .cover-band-chip {
        display: inline-block;
        margin-top: 0.18in;
        padding: 0.4em 1.1em;
        border-radius: 999px;
        background: {{ band_colour }};
        color: #ffffff;
        font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace;
        font-size: 11pt;
        font-weight: 400;
        letter-spacing: 0.18em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
      }
      .cover-score-label {
        margin-top: 0.16in;
        font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace;
        font-size: 7.5pt;
        letter-spacing: 0.2em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        color: var(--ink-subtle);
      }
      .cover-explain {
        margin: 0.34in 0 0;
        max-width: 5.4in;
        font-size: 10.5pt;
        line-height: 1.6;
        color: var(--ink-muted);
      }
      .cover-explain strong { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 700; }
      .cover-meta {
        position: absolute;
        bottom: 0;
        left: 0; right: 0;
        border-top: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
        padding-top: 0.22in;
      }
      .cover-meta table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; }
      .cover-meta td {
        vertical-align: top;
        padding: 0 0.3in 0.1in 0;
        border: none;
      }
      .cover-meta .k {
        font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace;
        font-size: 6.8pt;
        letter-spacing: 0.16em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        color: var(--ink-subtle);
        display: block;
        margin-bottom: 0.2em;
      }
      .cover-meta .v {
        font-size: 9pt;
        color: var(--ink);
      }
      .cover-meta .v.mono { font-size: 8.2pt; }

      /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ *
       * KPI card row                                                       *
       * ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
      .kpi-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: separate; border-spacing: 7px 0; margin: 0.2em 0 0.4em; }
      .kpi-table td {
        width: 16.6%;
        vertical-align: top;
        background: var(--card);
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-radius: 8px;
        padding: 11px 12px 12px;
      }
      .kpi-label {
        font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace;
        font-size: 6.8pt;
        letter-spacing: 0.16em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        color: var(--ink-subtle);
        margin-bottom: 0.5em;
      }
      .kpi-value {
        font-family: "Source Serif Pro", "Georgia", serif;
        font-size: 21pt;
        font-weight: 600;
        line-height: 1;
        color: var(--ink);
        letter-spacing: -0.02em;
      }
      .kpi-value .unit { font-size: 11pt; color: var(--ink-subtle); }
      .kpi-sub {
        margin-top: 0.55em;
        font-size: 7.5pt;
        color: var(--ink-muted);
        font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace;
        letter-spacing: 0.04em;
        white-space: nowrap;
      }
      /* stacked, legible severity breakdown (replaces the cramped one-liner) */
      .sev-stack { margin-top: 0.45em; }
      .sev-stack .srow {
        display: block;
        font-size: 8pt;
        line-height: 1.65;
        color: var(--ink-muted);
        white-space: nowrap;
      }
      .sev-stack .srow b { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 700; }
      .sev-stack .d {
        display: inline-block;
        width: 7px; height: 7px; border-radius: 2px;
        margin-right: 5px; vertical-align: middle;
      }
      .sev-stack .d-crit { background: var(--crit); }
      .sev-stack .d-high { background: var(--high); }
      .sev-stack .d-med  { background: var(--med); }
      .sev-stack .d-low  { background: var(--low); }
      /* stacked severity micro-bar inside FINDINGS kpi */
      .sevbar { margin-top: 0.6em; height: 6px; border-radius: 3px; overflow: hidden; background: var(--sunken); width: 100%; }
      .sevbar span { display: inline-block; height: 6px; vertical-align: top; }
      .sevbar .s-crit { background: var(--crit); }
      .sevbar .s-high { background: var(--high); }
      .sevbar .s-med  { background: var(--med); }
      .sevbar .s-low  { background: var(--low); }
      /* coverage pip grid */
      .pipgrid { margin-top: 0.6em; }
      .pip {
        display: inline-block; width: 8px; height: 8px; border-radius: 2px;
        background: var(--sunken); border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
        margin: 0 2px 0 0;
      }
      .pip.on { background: var(--brand); border-color: var(--brand); }

      /* Posture callout */
      .posture {
        background: var(--card);
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-left: 4px solid {{ band_colour }};
        border-radius: 8px;
        padding: 16px 18px;
        margin: 0 0 1.1em;
      }
      .posture p { margin: 0; font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink); }
      .posture .verdict { font-weight: 700; color: {{ band_colour }}; }

      /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ *
       * Definition / data tables                                           *
       * ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
      .deftable {
        width: 100%;
        border-collapse: collapse;
        background: var(--card);
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-radius: 8px;
        margin: 0 0 0.9em;
        overflow: hidden;
      }
      .deftable td {
        padding: 7px 12px;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
        vertical-align: top;
        font-size: 9pt;
      }
      .deftable tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }
      .deftable .k {
        width: 38%;
        color: var(--ink-muted);
        font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace;
        font-size: 7.6pt;
        letter-spacing: 0.06em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
      }
      .deftable .v { color: var(--ink); }
      .deftable .v.mono { font-size: 8.4pt; }

      /* two side-by-side plan tables via a layout table */
      .plan-grid { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; }
      .plan-grid > td { vertical-align: top; padding: 0; border: none; }
      .plan-grid .gap { width: 14px; padding: 0; border: none; }
      .plan-cap {
        font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace;
        font-size: 7pt; letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase;
        color: var(--brand-strong); margin: 0 0 0.4em 0.1em;
      }

      /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ *
       * ASI coverage table                                                 *
       * ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
      .asi-table {
        width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse;
        background: var(--card);
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden;
        margin: 0 0 0.6em;
      }
      .asi-table thead th {
        background: var(--sunken);
        font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace;
        font-size: 6.8pt; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase;
        color: var(--ink-muted); font-weight: 400;
        text-align: left; padding: 8px 12px;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
      }
      .asi-table thead th.num { text-align: right; }
      .asi-table td {
        padding: 8px 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
        vertical-align: middle; font-size: 9pt;
      }
      .asi-table tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }
      .asi-table td.id { font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace; font-size: 8.4pt; font-weight: 700; color: var(--ink); white-space: nowrap; }
      .asi-table td.desc { color: var(--ink); }
      .asi-table td.num { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
      .asi-table td.cnt { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; color: var(--ink-muted); }
      .asi-table tr.has-find td.cnt { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 700; }
      /* severity-tinted left edge per row */
      /* per-row score bar */
      .scorebar-wrap { display: block; width: 1.5in; }
      .scorebar {
        height: 6px; border-radius: 3px; background: var(--sunken);
        width: 100%; overflow: hidden; margin-top: 3px;
      }
      .scorebar > span { display: block; height: 6px; background: var(--brand); border-radius: 3px; }
      .scorebar.hot > span { background: var(--crit); }
      .scorebar.warm > span { background: var(--high); }
      .score-num { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; font-weight: 700; }

      /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ *
       * Finding cards                                                      *
       * ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
      .find {
        page-break-inside: avoid;
        background: var(--card);
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-radius: 12px;
        margin: 0 0 18px;
        overflow: hidden;
      }
      /* severity color spine via left border */
      .find.sev-critical { border-left: 5px solid var(--crit); }
      .find.sev-high     { border-left: 5px solid var(--high); }
      .find.sev-medium   { border-left: 5px solid var(--med); }
      .find.sev-low      { border-left: 5px solid var(--low); }
      .find.sev-info     { border-left: 5px solid var(--info); }

      .find-head { padding: 12px 15px 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
      .find-eyebrow {
        font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace;
        font-size: 7pt; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase;
        color: var(--ink-subtle); margin-bottom: 0.5em;
      }
      .find-title {
        font-family: "Source Serif Pro", "Georgia", serif;
        font-size: 12.5pt; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.25;
        color: var(--ink); margin: 0;
      }
      .find-summary { margin: 0.5em 0 0; font-size: 9pt; color: var(--ink-muted); line-height: 1.55; }

      /* chips */
      .chip {
        display: inline-block;
        padding: 0.18em 0.6em;
        border-radius: 4px;
        font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace;
        font-size: 7pt; letter-spacing: 0.04em;
        margin: 0 4px 4px 0;
        border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
        background: var(--sunken);
        color: var(--ink-muted);
        white-space: nowrap;
      }
      .chip .lab { color: var(--ink-subtle); }
      .chip-sev {
        border: none; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase;
      }
      .chip-sev.sev-critical { background: var(--crit-bg); color: var(--crit); }
      .chip-sev.sev-high     { background: var(--high-bg); color: var(--high); }
      .chip-sev.sev-medium   { background: var(--med-bg);  color: var(--med); }
      .chip-sev.sev-low      { background: var(--low-bg);  color: var(--low); }
      .chip-sev.sev-info     { background: #eff6ff;        color: var(--info); }
      .chip-asi   { background: var(--brand-tint); color: var(--brand-strong); border-color: #e3d9ff; }
      .chip-verdict { background: #eef2ff; color: #4338ca; border-color: #e0e3f5; }
      .chip-row { padding: 9px 15px 5px; }

      /* evidence mono block */
      .evidence { padding: 4px 15px 14px; }
      .ev-label {
        font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace;
        font-size: 6.8pt; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase;
        color: var(--ink-subtle); margin: 9px 0 3px;
      }
      .ev-block {
        background: var(--sunken);
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-radius: 8px;
        padding: 10px 12px;
        font-family: "JetBrains Mono", "Menlo", monospace;
        font-size: 8pt;
        line-height: 1.55;
        color: var(--ink);
        white-space: pre-wrap;
        word-break: break-word;
      }
      .ev-block.prompt { border-left: 3px solid var(--brand); }
      .ev-block.response { border-left: 3px solid var(--ink-subtle); }
      .ev-empty { font-style: italic; color: var(--ink-subtle); }

      .group-head {
        font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace;
        font-size: 7.5pt; letter-spacing: 0.18em; text-transform: uppercase;
        color: var(--ink-muted);
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
        padding-bottom: 0.35em; margin: 1.1em 0 0.8em;
      }
      .group-head .gcount { color: var(--ink-subtle); }
      .group-head.g-crit { color: var(--crit); }
      .group-head.g-high { color: var(--high); }
      .group-head.g-med  { color: var(--med); }
      .group-head.g-low  { color: var(--low); }

      .empty-state {
        background: var(--low-bg);
        border: 1px solid #d9efb5;
        border-radius: 8px;
        padding: 18px 20px;
        color: #3f6212;
        font-size: 10pt;
      }

      /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ *
       * Appendices                                                         *
       * ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
      .appendix { padding-top: 0.2in; }
      .appendix h2 { font-size: 15pt; }
      .appendix h3 { font-size: 11pt; margin: 1.1em 0 0.4em; }
      .appendix p, .appendix li { font-size: 8.8pt; color: var(--ink-muted); line-height: 1.55; }
      .appendix-tag {
        font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace;
        font-size: 7pt; letter-spacing: 0.2em; text-transform: uppercase;
        color: var(--brand-strong); margin-bottom: 0.3em;
      }
      .map-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; background: var(--card);
        border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; margin: 0.5em 0 1em; }
      .map-table thead th {
        background: var(--sunken);
        font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace;
        font-size: 6.4pt; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase;
        color: var(--ink-muted); font-weight: 400; text-align: left;
        padding: 7px 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
      }
      .map-table td { padding: 6px 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); font-size: 8pt; vertical-align: top; }
      .map-table tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }
      .map-table td.id { font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace; font-weight: 700; white-space: nowrap; }
      .map-table .mono { font-size: 7.4pt; }
      .receipt-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; background: var(--card);
        border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; margin: 0.5em 0 1em; }
      .receipt-table td { padding: 7px 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); font-size: 8.4pt; vertical-align: top; }
      .receipt-table tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }
      .receipt-table .k {
        width: 34%; font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace; font-size: 7.4pt;
        letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-muted);
      }
      .receipt-table code { font-size: 7.8pt; color: var(--ink); }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>

    {# ---- derive severity counts + KPI values inline from findings ---- #}
    {% set ns = namespace(crit=0, high=0, med=0, low=0, info=0) %}
    {% for f in findings %}
      {% set sv = (f.severity_label if f.severity_label is defined and f.severity_label else f.severity.value)|lower %}
      {% if sv == 'critical' %}{% set ns.crit = ns.crit + 1 %}
      {% elif sv == 'high' %}{% set ns.high = ns.high + 1 %}
      {% elif sv == 'medium' %}{% set ns.med = ns.med + 1 %}
      {% elif sv == 'low' %}{% set ns.low = ns.low + 1 %}
      {% else %}{% set ns.info = ns.info + 1 %}{% endif %}
    {% endfor %}
    {% set total = findings|length %}
    {% set asi_covered = (findings | map(attribute='asi') | map(attribute='value') | list | unique | list | length) %}
    {% set elapsed = scan.duration_seconds | default(0, true) %}
    {% set mm = (elapsed // 60) | int %}
    {% set ss = (elapsed % 60) | int %}
    {% set cost = scan.cost_usd | default(0, true) %}
    {% set scored = (scan.scoring_valid if scan.scoring_valid is defined else (scan.aivss is not none)) %}

    <!-- ======================== 1. COVER ======================== -->
    <section class="cover">
      <div class="cover-inner">
        <div class="cover-rule"></div>
        <div class="cover-mark">AGENT<span class="dot">·</span>GUARDIAN</div>
        <div class="cover-kicker">Adversarial AI Security Assessment</div>

        <h1 class="cover-title">Agentic Threat Posture Report</h1>

        <div class="cover-score-wrap">
          <div class="cover-score">{% if scored %}{{ scan.aivss }}<span class="denom"> / 100</span>{% else %}<span class="denom" style="font-size:34pt">N/A</span>{% endif %}</div>
          <div>
            <span class="cover-band-chip">{{ scan.band.value }}</span>
          </div>
          <div class="cover-score-label">AIVSS · AI Vulnerability Scoring System</div>
        </div>

        {# Plain-language explanation of what the score + band mean. #}
        {% set bk = (scan.band.value | lower) %}
        <p class="cover-explain">
          AIVSS rates this agent's resilience from <strong>0</strong> (fully exploitable) to
          <strong>100</strong> (fully defended) — higher is safer.
          {% if scored %}
            A score of <strong>{{ scan.aivss }}</strong> puts it in the <strong>{{ scan.band.value }}</strong> band:
            {% if bk == 'excellent' %}strong resilience — it defended nearly every adversarial attempt.
            {% elif bk == 'good' %}solid resilience, with a few gaps worth closing.
            {% elif bk == 'warning' %}notable weaknesses that need attention before broad use.
            {% elif bk == 'poor' %}serious, exploitable weaknesses — fix these before exposing this agent to untrusted input.
            {% elif bk == 'critical' %}severe, readily exploitable weaknesses — do not expose this agent to untrusted input until fixed.
            {% else %}see the findings below for per-category detail.{% endif %}
          {% else %}
            This run used a non-authoritative evaluator, so no trustworthy composite score was produced — see the findings below.
          {% endif %}
        </p>

        <div class="cover-meta">
          <table>
            <tr>
              <td>
                <span class="k">Target</span>
                <span class="v mono">{{ scan.target_ref }}</span>
              </td>
              <td>
                <span class="k">Tier</span>
                <span class="v">{{ scan.tier.value }}</span>
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>
                <span class="k">Generated</span>
                <span class="v">{{ scan.created_at.strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M UTC') if scan.created_at.strftime is defined else scan.created_at }}</span>
              </td>
              <td>
                <span class="k">Findings</span>
                <span class="v">{{ total }}</span>
              </td>
            </tr>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ==================== 2. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY ==================== -->
    <section class="block">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="eyebrow">Section 01 — Executive Summary</div>
        <h2>Security posture at a glance</h2>
        <p class="lede">Adversarial swarm assessment of the target's resilience against the OWASP Agentic Security Initiative (ASI) Top&nbsp;10 threat classes, scored on the AI Vulnerability Scoring System.</p>
      </div>

      {# KPI card row — 6 tiles #}
      <table class="kpi-table">
        <tr>
          <td>
            <div class="kpi-label">AIVSS</div>
            <div class="kpi-value">{% if scored %}{{ scan.aivss }}{% else %}—{% endif %}</div>
            <div class="kpi-sub">{{ scan.band.value }}</div>
          </td>
          <td>
            <div class="kpi-label">Findings</div>
            <div class="kpi-value">{{ total }}</div>
            <div class="sevbar">
              {% if total %}
                <span class="s-crit" style="width:{{ (ns.crit / total * 100) | round(1) }}%"></span><span class="s-high" style="width:{{ (ns.high / total * 100) | round(1) }}%"></span><span class="s-med" style="width:{{ (ns.med / total * 100) | round(1) }}%"></span><span class="s-low" style="width:{{ (ns.low / total * 100) | round(1) }}%"></span>
              {% endif %}
            </div>
          </td>
          <td>
            <div class="kpi-label">By severity</div>
            <div class="sev-stack">
              <span class="srow"><i class="d d-crit"></i><b>{{ ns.crit }}</b> Critical</span>
              <span class="srow"><i class="d d-high"></i><b>{{ ns.high }}</b> High</span>
              <span class="srow"><i class="d d-med"></i><b>{{ ns.med }}</b> Medium</span>
              <span class="srow"><i class="d d-low"></i><b>{{ ns.low }}</b> Low</span>
            </div>
          </td>
          <td>
            <div class="kpi-label">Coverage</div>
            <div class="kpi-value">{{ asi_covered }}<span class="unit"> / 10</span></div>
            <div class="pipgrid">
              {% for i in range(10) %}<span class="pip {{ 'on' if i < asi_covered else '' }}"></span>{% endfor %}
            </div>
          </td>
          <td>
            <div class="kpi-label">Cost</div>
            <div class="kpi-value"><span class="unit">$</span>{{ "%.2f"|format(cost) }}</div>
            <div class="kpi-sub">{{ "{:,}".format(scan.tokens_total) if scan.tokens_total is defined and scan.tokens_total else '—' }} tok</div>
          </td>
          <td>
            <div class="kpi-label">Elapsed</div>
            <div class="kpi-value">{{ "%d:%02d"|format(mm, ss) }}</div>
            <div class="kpi-sub">{{ "%.1f"|format(elapsed) }}s wall-clock</div>
          </td>
        </tr>
      </table>
    </section>

    <!-- ======================== 3. OVERVIEW ======================== -->
    <section class="block">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="eyebrow">Section 02 — Overview</div>
        <h2>Scan plan &amp; attack-surface coverage</h2>
        <p class="lede">The configuration that produced this assessment, followed by per-category exposure across the OWASP ASI Top&nbsp;10.</p>
      </div>

      {# scan-plan definition tables, two columns via layout table #}
      <table class="plan-grid">
        <td>
          <div class="plan-cap">Target &amp; Mode</div>
          <table class="deftable">
            <tr><td class="k">Target</td><td class="v mono">{{ scan.target_ref }}</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="k">Mode</td><td class="v">{{ scan.target_mode }}</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="k">Run mode</td><td class="v">{{ scan.mode | default('—', true) }}</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="k">Tier</td><td class="v">{{ scan.tier.value }}</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="k">Reachable</td><td class="v">{{ '✓ reachable' if scored else '—' }}</td></tr>
          </table>

          <div class="plan-cap">Models</div>
          <table class="deftable">
            <tr><td class="k">Attacker</td><td class="v mono">{{ scan.engine.get('attacker', '—') if scan.engine else '—' }}</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="k">Evaluator</td><td class="v mono">{{ scan.engine.get('evaluator', '—') if scan.engine else '—' }}</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="k">Commander</td><td class="v mono">{{ scan.engine.get('commander', '—') if scan.engine else '—' }}</td></tr>
          </table>
        </td>
        <td class="gap"></td>
        <td>
          <div class="plan-cap">Budget</div>
          <table class="deftable">
            <tr><td class="k">Wall-clock cap</td><td class="v">uncapped</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="k">USD cap</td><td class="v">uncapped</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="k">Actual cost</td><td class="v">${{ "%.4f"|format(cost) }}</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="k">Tokens</td><td class="v">{{ "{:,}".format(scan.tokens_total) if scan.tokens_total is defined and scan.tokens_total else '—' }}</td></tr>
          </table>

          <div class="plan-cap">Safety Guards</div>
          <table class="deftable">
            <tr><td class="k">RoE blocklist</td><td class="v">none observed</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="k">Authorization</td><td class="v">n/a</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="k">Egress policy</td><td class="v">unrestricted</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="k">Output format</td><td class="v mono">json</td></tr>
          </table>
        </td>
      </table>

      {# ASI coverage table #}
      <div class="plan-cap" style="margin-top:0.5em;">OWASP ASI Top 10 — Attack-Surface Coverage</div>
      <table class="asi-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th style="width:12%">ASI</th>
            <th>Threat class</th>
            <th class="num" style="width:24%">Resilience score</th>
            <th class="num" style="width:12%">Findings</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for row in asi_rows %}
          {% set sc = row.score | default(0, true) %}
          <tr class="{{ 'has-find' if row.count else '' }}">
            <td class="id">{{ row.id }}</td>
            <td class="desc">{{ row.description }}</td>
            <td class="num">
              <span class="score-num">{{ "%.1f"|format(sc) }}</span>
              <span class="scorebar-wrap">
                <span class="scorebar {{ 'hot' if sc < 40 else ('warm' if sc < 70 else '') }}"><span style="width:{{ sc | round(0) }}%"></span></span>
              </span>
            </td>
            <td class="cnt">{{ row.count }}</td>
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="subtle" style="font-size:7.6pt; margin-top:0.4em;">Resilience score is the per-category AIVSS sub-score (0–100, higher = stronger / less exposed). The score bar turns amber below 70 and red below 40 to flag weaker resilience.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- ======================== 4. FINDINGS ======================== -->
    <section class="block">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="eyebrow">Section 03 — Findings</div>
        <h2>Confirmed exposures</h2>
        <p class="lede">Each card records a judge-confirmed adversarial outcome with its framework classification and the triggering evidence. Findings are grouped by severity, then ordered by ASI category.</p>
      </div>

      {% if findings %}
        {# Group by severity in fixed order, then ASI. #}
        {% set order = [('critical','g-crit','Critical'), ('high','g-high','High'), ('medium','g-med','Medium'), ('low','g-low','Low'), ('info','','Informational')] %}
        {% for sev_key, gcls, sev_name in order %}
          {# collect findings in this severity bucket (inline filter) #}
          {% set matched = [] %}
          {% for f in findings %}
            {% set sv = (f.severity_label if f.severity_label is defined and f.severity_label else f.severity.value)|lower %}
            {% if sv == sev_key or (sev_key == 'info' and sv not in ['critical','high','medium','low']) %}
              {% set _ = matched.append(f) %}
            {% endif %}
          {% endfor %}
          {% if matched %}
          <div class="group-head {{ gcls }}">{{ sev_name }} severity <span class="gcount">· {{ matched|length }} finding{{ '' if matched|length == 1 else 's' }}</span></div>

          {% for f in (matched | sort(attribute='asi.value')) %}
            {% set sevc = 'sev-' ~ ((f.severity_label if f.severity_label is defined and f.severity_label else f.severity.value)|lower) %}
            {% if sevc not in ['sev-critical','sev-high','sev-medium','sev-low','sev-info'] %}{% set sevc = 'sev-info' %}{% endif %}
          <div class="find {{ sevc }}">
            <div class="find-head">
              <div class="find-eyebrow">{{ f.asi.value }} · {{ f.csa_category.value if f.csa_category else 'uncategorized' }}</div>
              {% set f_title = (f.title if f.title is defined and f.title else None) %}
              <h3 class="find-title">{{ f_title or f.summary or 'Adversarial outcome confirmed' }}</h3>
              {# Only show the summary as a sub-line when it is genuinely distinct
                 from the title (the Finding model usually carries only `summary`,
                 so rendering both would duplicate the same sentence). #}
              {% if f_title and f.summary and f.summary != f_title %}
              <p class="find-summary">{{ f.summary }}</p>
              {% endif %}
            </div>

            <div class="chip-row">
              <span class="chip chip-sev {{ sevc }}">{{ (f.severity_label if f.severity_label is defined and f.severity_label else f.severity.value)|upper }}</span>
              <span class="chip chip-asi">{{ f.asi.value }}</span>
              {% if f.csa_category %}<span class="chip"><span class="lab">CSA</span> {{ f.csa_category.value }}</span>{% endif %}
              {% for technique in (f.mitre_atlas or []) %}<span class="chip"><span class="lab">ATLAS</span> {{ technique }}</span>{% endfor %}
            </div>

            <div class="evidence">
              <div class="ev-label">Attacker prompt</div>
              {% if f.trigger_prompt %}
                <div class="ev-block prompt">{{ f.trigger_prompt | truncate(700, True, ' …') }}</div>
              {% else %}
                <div class="ev-block prompt ev-empty">No prompt captured (PII-redacted scan).</div>
              {% endif %}
              <div class="ev-label">Target response</div>
              {% if f.trigger_response %}
                <div class="ev-block response">{{ f.trigger_response | truncate(700, True, ' …') }}</div>
              {% else %}
                <div class="ev-block response ev-empty">No response captured (PII-redacted scan).</div>
              {% endif %}
            </div>
          </div>
          {% endfor %}
          {% endif %}
        {% endfor %}
      {% else %}
        <div class="empty-state">
          <strong>No findings.</strong> The target defended every adversarial attempt within the configured budget. This is a strong signal, though absence of findings is not proof of absence of vulnerability — re-run at a higher tier for deeper coverage.
        </div>
      {% endif %}
    </section>

    <!-- ======================== 5. APPENDICES ======================== -->
    <section class="block appendix">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="appendix-tag">Appendix A</div>
        <h2>Triple-framework mapping</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        AgentGuardian tags every finding against three industry frameworks: OWASP ASI 2026
        (Top 10 for Agentic Applications), MITRE ATLAS v5.4.0 (Adversarial Threat Landscape for
        AI Systems), and the CSA Agentic AI Red Teaming Guide (Huang et al., 2025-05-28). The
        mapping below shows the primary ATLAS techniques and CSA categories each ASI bucket exercises.
      </p>
      <table class="map-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th style="width:10%">ASI</th><th style="width:22%">OWASP category</th><th>Primary MITRE ATLAS technique(s)</th><th style="width:24%">CSA category</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td class="id">ASI01</td><td>Goal Hijack</td><td><span class="mono">AML.T0051</span>, <span class="mono">AML.T0054</span></td><td>goal-instruction-manipulation</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="id">ASI02</td><td>Tool Misuse</td><td><span class="mono">AML.T0053</span>, Publish Poisoned AI Agent Tool</td><td>authorization-control-hijacking</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="id">ASI03</td><td>Privilege Abuse</td><td><span class="mono">AML.T0049</span>, Escape to Host</td><td>authorization-control-hijacking</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="id">ASI04</td><td>Supply Chain</td><td><span class="mono">AML.T0010</span>, <span class="mono">AML.T0011</span></td><td>supply-chain-dependency</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="id">ASI05</td><td>Code Execution</td><td><span class="mono">AML.T0050</span>, Escape to Host</td><td>agent-critical-system-interaction</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="id">ASI06</td><td>Memory Poisoning</td><td><span class="mono">AML.T0070</span>, AI Agent Context Poisoning</td><td>memory-context-manipulation</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="id">ASI07</td><td>Agent-to-Agent (A2A)</td><td><span class="mono">AML.T0048</span>, Inter-Agent Manipulation</td><td>multi-agent-exploitation</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="id">ASI08</td><td>Cascading Failures</td><td><span class="mono">AML.T0034</span>, <span class="mono">AML.T0029</span></td><td>impact-chain-blast-radius</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="id">ASI09</td><td>Trust Exploitation</td><td><span class="mono">AML.T0051.000</span>, <span class="mono">AML.T0052</span></td><td>checker-out-of-the-loop</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="id">ASI10</td><td>Rogue Agents (drift)</td><td><span class="mono">AML.T0046</span>, AI Agent Goal Drift</td><td>hallucination-exploitation</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <div class="section-head" style="margin-top:1.4em;">
        <div class="appendix-tag">Appendix B</div>
        <h2>Methodology &amp; bibliography</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        Each of the 10 ASI specialist agents extends its seed probes dynamically using four
        published adversarial strategies. Selection is bandit-driven: AgentGuardian's strategy
        router keeps the per-(target, ASI) success rates in shared memory and biases later
        attempts toward strategies that succeeded earlier in the run.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>TAP</strong> — Tree of Attacks with Pruning; tree-of-thoughts jailbreak with on-topic pruning (Mehrotra et al., 2024).</li>
        <li><strong>Crescendo</strong> — Multi-turn benign-to-harmful ramp (Russinovich et al., 2025).</li>
        <li><strong>MAD-MAX</strong> — Multi-agent adversarial dialogue with mode exploitation (Schoepf et al., 2025).</li>
        <li><strong>PAIR</strong> — Prompt Automatic Iterative Refinement; attacker LLM critiques and rewrites (Chao et al., 2023).</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The Layer-2 judge LLM evaluates each transcript against a category-specific rubric and
        emits a structured verdict; agreement with human reviewers is calibrated against the
        evaluation harness described in Chen et al. (2024). For the full bibliography and
        per-probe references see <code>docs/arxiv-preprint.md</code>.
      </p>

      <div class="section-head" style="margin-top:1.4em;">
        <div class="appendix-tag">Appendix C</div>
        <h2>Reproducibility receipt</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        This receipt records the configuration that produced the scan above. Re-running
        AgentGuardian with these inputs against the same target should produce a deterministic
        AIVSS score (modulo non-determinism in third-party LLM endpoints).
      </p>
      <table class="receipt-table">
        <tr><td class="k">Scan ID</td><td><code>{{ scan.id }}</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="k">Scan timestamp</td><td><code>{{ scan.created_at.isoformat() if scan.created_at.isoformat is defined else scan.created_at }}</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="k">Target mode</td><td><code>{{ scan.target_mode }}</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="k">Target ref</td><td><code>{{ scan.target_ref }}</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="k">Tier</td><td><code>{{ scan.tier.value }}</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="k">Run mode</td><td><code>{{ scan.mode | default('—', true) }}</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="k">Commander model</td><td><code>{{ scan.engine.get('commander', 'not recorded') if scan.engine else 'not recorded' }}</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="k">Attacker model</td><td><code>{{ scan.engine.get('attacker', 'not recorded') if scan.engine else 'not recorded' }}</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="k">Evaluator model</td><td><code>{{ scan.engine.get('evaluator', 'not recorded') if scan.engine else 'not recorded' }}</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td class="k">Signature algorithm</td><td><code>Ed25519 + HMAC-SHA256</code></td></tr>
      </table>
      <p>
        This PDF is a visualisation of the canonical JSON report. Use
        <code>agent-guardian verify &lt;report.json&gt;</code> to verify the HMAC-SHA256 and
        Ed25519 signatures on the source artefact.
      </p>
    </section>

  </body>
</html>
